@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# AUTHKIT-1 — external human login through WorkOS AuthKit
+
+Base: `4534324173e0c8f7e2844c86da60795c32d93da9`.
+
+This round adds the hosted authorization redirect, a server-side authorization-
code exchange,
+offline RS256 verification against the WorkOS client's kid-indexed JWKS, and th
e shared session
+establishment seam. It does not create Memberships and adds no UI.
+
+## Modules
+
+<!-- MODULE: CommonplaceNext.WorkOS.KeySource -->
+<!-- MODULE: CommonplaceNext.WorkOS.Login -->
+<!-- MODULE: CommonplaceNext.Web.WorkOSController -->
+
+`WorkOS.KeySource` is a named second instance of `CloudflareAccess.KeySource`;
the shared cache was
+parameterised by registered name rather than copied. Both instances select keys
 by kid membership.
+
+`AssertionVerifier` has one new, explicit `provider: :workos` profile. Only tha
t profile omits the
+Cloudflare-only `aud`, `type`, and `nbf` requirements. With no provider option,
 the existing Access
+profile and its exact option set remain strict. WorkOS supplies no audience cla
im.
+
+`Session.establish/2` is the public tail extracted from `Session.authenticate/1
`. Both providers
+therefore converge on the existing single private principal sink; there is no s
econd session-login
+writer.
+
+Production reads the client id, API key, issuer, and redirect URI at runtime. T
he client id and API
+key have no defaults and an absent value raises naming the environment variable
. Dev and test have
+no WorkOS configuration and answer `not_configured` without starting a network
client.
+
+## Arms
+
+<!-- ARM: code exchange records one form POST and its token verifies as a WorkO
S human -->
+<!-- ARM: signed by a kid absent from the fixture JWKS is unknown -->
+<!-- ARM: WorkOS token with a different issuer is refused -->
+<!-- ARM: expired WorkOS token is refused -->
+<!-- ARM: callback state mismatch returns 401 and establishes no login session
-->
+<!-- ARM: default Access profile still refuses a token missing audience -->
+<!-- ARM: production configuration raises naming WORKOS_API_KEY when it is abse
nt -->
+<!-- ARM: unconfigured WorkOS login route returns named not configured 404 -->
+
+The repository plan-arm gate, formatter check, warnings-as-errors compile, and
captured full suite
+are the K9 landing checks. The sandbox has no WorkOS credentials and network ca
lls are prohibited,
+so it cannot perform a real code exchange or real JWKS fetch. The reviewer perf
orms that decisive
+live check on the credentialed host.
